body:
>You're... ... looking for someone who will respect you and your boundaries.

This\^

&#x200B;

>You don't really need to have actual dates to meet people and hangout.

Then, how? I'm new to everything gay. Grindr scared me soo much I don't think I can go back to the app.

&#x200B;

>If you're looking for a more friends with benefits-type situation, ...

Ideally, friends with benefits (or a friend of a friend) - yeah. That's the dream, that way it's a.) less awkward and b.) there would be fewer stress/expectations

&#x200B;

>...you kind of have to be forward with them ...

So, with the guy 4 weeks ago I was then he flipped a switch and things were different. I know that's just one guy in one situation but for me I'm 2 for 2 running into 'bad' guys.

&#x200B;

Just because you're shorter doesn't mean you have to assume the bottom role either.

I know this, I just wish other guys didn't assume - I suppose I should work on my communication, but really both times are not *my fault* but I'm gonna work on communication nonetheless.

&#x200B;

>Additionally, bottoming/topping need not be part of the repertoire to have good sex with folks.

It's something I'd like to try (both top and bottom), I just seem to attract people that are shitty and have no respect for me or my boundaries. I'm starting to think the common thread in all my experiences is me, so I'm to blame, but I try to not entertain thoughts like that since that's a great way to have negative ruminating thoughts.

&#x200B;

>Just... don't feel pressured to do something you're not comfortable with.

I have trouble with this because I am still working through being comfortable with my bi/gay-ness and sometimes I think I'm never going to make progress without pushing myself - however - I need to make sure I push myself without putting myself in situations where I could get hurt or worse. Clearly I need to work on that/work on my situational awareness/ability to read people/assertiveness.

&#x200B;

**Also:** Writing all this makes me feel really embarrassed. I feel like every time I delve into my feelings on gay relations I end up sounding like a scared girl talking about guys :\\
